Licence compatibility with GPL-3.0-or-later (a good-faith reading, NOT legal advice or a legal guarantee)
  qrcodegen (MIT), zlib (zlib licence), LZMA SDK LzmaDec (public domain), font8x8 (public domain): permissive, generally
  regarded as GPLv3-compatible (the FSF lists MIT/Expat and zlib as GPL-compatible). Keep their notices.
  zstd: dual-licensed BSD-3-Clause / GPL-2.0-only. We use the BSD-3-Clause option only (GPLv2-only would NOT be
  GPLv3-compatible, so do not rely on that option). BSD-3-Clause is GPLv3-compatible.
  uwp-crossbuild (MIT): a build tool fetched at setup time, not shipped or linked into our binaries.
  Boxedwine (GPL-2.0-or-later): compatible via "or later" (see above); not shipped. Check the exact per-file headers
  before reusing any file, since a file stating "version 2 only" would not be.
  Wine (LGPL-2.1-or-later): fine to build and use alongside GPLv3 code; keep its licence texts with any DLLs you redistribute
  and offer the corresponding source (the pinned tarball). We do not redistribute Wine binaries from this repository.
  Microsoft SDK/CRT (via xwin): downloaded under Microsoft's terms at build time, not distributed here.
  If you add third-party code, list it here and check its licence first.

Reference only (no code copied)
  Wine (LGPL-2.1-or-later): its *.spec export lists are used as a checklist; research/ and src/tools/xbox/wine_gap*.py read
  a local Wine checkout/build to produce coverage tables of function names. No Wine source is included.

Generated data: the Direct3D triangle shader bytecode in src/xbox-test/uwph/host/shaders/ is compiled from our own
